? What is a frame in an animation?
+ One image in the sequence
- The entire movie file
- The sound playback rate
- A colour lookup table
= Frames are displayed in sequence to suggest change.

? What does fps measure?
+ Frames displayed per second
- Pixels displayed per scene
- Files produced per script
- Fonts positioned per screen
= Frame rate is measured in frames per second.

? Which method updates changes after an initial frame?
+ Delta-frame animation
- Full-frame replacement only
- Static vector illustration
- Single-picture typography
= Delta refers to the difference between frames.

? What changes in palette animation?
+ Colours or colour-table entries
- Only the physical display size
- Only a character voice recording
- Only the file extension name
= Colour changes can suggest animation without moving geometry.

? What does a keyframe record?
+ An important state or pose
- Every possible compressed file
- Only the application menu
- Only the background filename
= The animator sets important states; tweening fills gaps.

? What is tweening?
+ Generating intermediate states
- Deleting every second picture
- Changing the display hardware
- Recording only the final pose
= Tweens connect keyframes.

? Which animation is best described as an object following a route?
+ Path animation
- Shape morphing
- Palette cycling
- Static composition
= A path controls position along a route.

? A circle gradually becomes a triangle. Which technique is used?
+ Shape tween
- Audio mixing
- Frame cropping
- Layer renaming
= The outline geometry changes between key shapes.

? Why separate a moving character and a fixed background?
+ Reuse the background while editing movement
- Force background and character to share every movement
- Remove independent timing controls from every layer
- Prevent later colour adjustments to either visual element
= This is a useful cel/layer separation.

? Which parameter belongs primarily to timing?
+ Frame rate
- Stage width
- Colour mode
- Vector stroke colour
= Frame rate affects display timing.

? What should an impact sound align with?
+ The contact frame
- The filename change
- The menu opening
- The colour-profile dialog
= Synchronised sound reinforces the visible action.

? What does a reduced-motion rule support?
+ Users requesting less animation
- Only higher screen resolution
- Only additional music tracks
- Only larger compressed videos
= Respect the user preference and keep information accessible.
